comments.body:
> what is the scenario where you are compiling with Tensor input, but later providing ACT? Relaxing guard for this case feels suspect. The other way (ACT during tracing, Tensor during runtime) can be relaxed as the runtime wrapper handles unwrapping ACT.

@aditvenk  You're right - that direction doesn't actually happen in FSDP+TP. It was just my repro tracing in the wrong order.
The all-gather output is always an ACT. The plain Tensor only appears after it's awaited. So the first trace sees ACT, and later steps may hand in a resolved Tensor - the safe direction you described. I've fixed the repro to trace on ACT first, and the recompile now fires when the Tensor arrives, with identical output every step.
